OL,3,GNEWSAPlayground staff say they are
OL,4,Afighting 'tooth and nail' to stay open
OL,5,
OL,6,FCharities running staffed adventure
OL,7,Fplaygrounds say they are fighting
OL,8,F"tooth and nail" to stay open for
OL,9,Fchildren and their families.
OL,11,FBut operators of some of the
OL,12,Fspecialised spaces, often based in
OL,13,Flower-income communities, are fearful
OL,14,Ffor the future due to financial
OL,15,Fpressures and funding.
OL,17,FAt The Big Swing Adventure Playground
OL,18,Fin Bradford, six-year-old Benny is busy
OL,19,Fscaling a wooden fort before throwing
OL,20,Fhimself on to a pile of crash mats
OL,21,Fbelow.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
